 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+Cache replacement uses the 2Q eviction policy to resist sequential scan pollution while preserving frequently revisited comparison sheets:
+- **First-in FIFO queue ($A1in$)**: newly admitted sheets enter $A1in$, sized to a fraction of the cache (e.g., 25% of total capacity).
+- **Out-of-cache ghost references ($A1out$)**: sheets evicted from $A1in$ have their keys preserved in a bounded ghost FIFO queue ($A1out$) without holding file payload on disk.
+- **Main hot queue ($Am$)**: an LRU queue holding sheets proven to be reused (either accessed while in $A1in$ or re-requested while their key remains in $A1out$). When cache space is needed and $A1in$ exceeds its threshold, entries are evicted from $A1in$; otherwise, victim entries are evicted from the tail of $Am$.
+
+All replacement queues, ghost references, and eviction decisions remain entirely private to the preview worker.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Preview cache eviction policy | 2Q replacement policy | LRU, Frequency-based eviction with aging (LFU-aging) | Protects repeatedly reviewed comparison sheets from eviction during long sequential screenings without retaining obsolete entries indefinitely as frequency counters can. Tradeoff of dual-queue bookkeeping and ghost list tracking is contained entirely within the private preview cache. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+1. Eviction policy selection: 2Q chosen to prevent screening scan pollution while retaining comparison working sets.
+
+### Deferred
+1. Concrete tuning parameters for the $A1in$ / $Am$ capacity split and $A1out$ ghost reference limit (to be benchmarked against pilot workload).
